---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Does every automation project need AI?",
    answer:
      "No. Many business automations are better implemented using normal software rules. AI is useful where the process genuinely requires interpretation, language understanding, classification or generation.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can AI be integrated into our existing software?",
    answer:
      "Often, yes. If the existing system has suitable APIs, extension points or backend access, AI capabilities may be introduced without rebuilding the entire application.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can an AI system use our own business documents?",
    answer:
      "Yes, depending on the use case and data requirements. Systems can be designed to retrieve relevant information from controlled business sources rather than rely only on general model knowledge.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can AI responses always be trusted?",
    answer:
      "No. Generative models can produce incorrect or misleading outputs. Important workflows should include validation, controlled context, confidence boundaries or human review where appropriate.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKP build private internal AI assistants?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Internal assistants can be designed around defined users, business information and responsibilities, subject to the required data and security architecture.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Is AI expensive to run?",
    answer:
      "Cost depends on model choice, request volume, context size, infrastructure and the complexity of the workflow. Cost should be considered during solution design rather than after deployment.",
  },
];
---

<section class="ai-faq">
  <div class="site-container ai-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>AI solutions FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before adding AI to the workflow.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ai-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .ai-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .ai-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .ai-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .ai-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .ai-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .ai-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .ai-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .ai-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
